    "scientific_name": "Nemichthys scolopaceus",
    "habitat": "mesopelagic",
    "order": 52,
    "notes": "Thread-thin body up to ~1.4 m that ends in a long filament; very long bird-beak jaws that bow apart toward the tips and cannot close, lined with tiny hooked teeth; large eyes; low dorsal and anal fins running most of the body. Grey-brown back, darker belly. Drifts head-up or head-down and snags shrimp antennae on its jaws."
